INSERT INTO `do_files` VALUES (1,'2','sikapa','hXxZD2jj7+d8+twXZE6AYacRf4TGnRvuTRNnQrDU5uKPmleCCS6Prpy/YqVLOO7/ZJRCGySmKHlLh2ZsjsVkW6mdw+n0Uaa9FOKuh3c0iNWb2qQX5cX4ljY+FqBnPKf8C/OiGI6zCheyYOzS0GCWGA==','eqamRB5C24ArUYX0EXfkdw==','2026/08/23 19:21:59','medkey_1356054617','test_upload.txt','This is a test medical dataset file for Antigravity Proxy Re-Encryption testing.\n','htxvnHFTsxnbvqgREu1fa5O2aXvArYKJpplYIa','Ux1NLBKq35ST/Y9po8m8g+bqcRuf+b4U','ZpbwlABdhyn91xevaXahFkeLIo0FzjR+a','d21ec1f3cafa26cc127e2be8eb320615c1a22ed89346623cb235a90fd7430137','1deb6681ba499b15c145e8abe5b628b4ff4f439de6cb536bd3b58336356d6efa','6f0179e4a3f6d65318a812318707629532caa17e1cd72772862d2b4142232618','This is a test medical data\n','set file for Antigravity Pr\n','oxy Re-Encryption testing.\n','PLEhG9IGWXkhxaoUMIGjww==','/SL7m4FZoZyjpZq7c6CbEiD4UBZvQnHkPFpXtqqAW2CqqOUYOqROKVH/7opM6DEBoQDbbUtAc4cdeyJuMI831nlWaTrae7F+EFHmL2y6kybb6X+YDHTcF5ivFz6suyU2MnQgu6rhXJBxLWPIvybezQ==','0.0','0xe0b72c0ccc7e721c12b414644fd8b987290a948c67f9215d38eeb053e774638d'),(2,'2','sikapa','','oMLe4otuJdWjW/Xgb2qVYA==','2026/08/23 19:28:48','cnn','cnn.txt','Goal: Reduce crop losses, improve farmer decision-making, promote sustainable agriculture\n\n- AI and deep learning revolutionizing agriculture.\n- CNNs outperform traditional ML in disease classification.\n- Problem: Farmers struggle with disease identification ? yield loss, improper pesticide use.\n- Objective: Build a mobile CNN-based system for accurate disease detection and advisory.\n1\n\n\n- Traditional methods: SVM, KNN, image processing ? limited accuracy.\n- CNN breakthroughs: PlantVillage dataset, >99% accuracy under controlled conditions.\n- Transfer learning: ResNet, MobileNet, EfficientNet improve generalization.\n- MobileNetV2: lightweight, efficient, 98.7% accuracy for potato diseases (Pineda Medina et al., 2024).\n- Limitation: performance drops in real-world field images.\n\nSlide 4 û Methodology\n- Dataset: PlantVillage (2,500+ images, multiple crops).\n- Data split: 60:20:20 (train, validation, test).\n- Models: MobileNetV2 (89% accuracy), EfficientNet-B0 (91.2% accuracy).\n- Optimizers: SGD baseline, Adam for improved convergence.\n- Deployment: TensorFlow Lite for mobile inference.\n- Architecture: Image acquisition ? preprocessing ? CNN classification ? result visualization.\n\nSlide 5 û Significance of the Study\n- Agriculture = 32 billion cedis contribution to GhanaÆs GDP (2024).\n- Crop losses ~19.3% due to diseases/post-harvest issues.\n- System reduces losses, strengthens food security.\n- Empowers rural farmers with offline, AI-driven diagnostics.\n- Promotes sustainable farming practices.\n\nSlide 6 û Limitations\n- Dataset variability may not fully represent real-world conditions.\n- Mobile hardware constraints limit model complexity.\n- Advisory accuracy depends on dataset scope; rare diseases may be missed.\n- Farmer adoption may be affected by literacy and digital skills.\n- Controlled dataset accuracy may drop in field conditions.\n\nSlide 7 û Scope/Delimitation\n- Focus crops: corn, orange, pepper, potato, soybean, tomato.\n- Dataset source: filtered PlantVillage dataset.\n- Geographic scope: Ghana and West Africa, targeting rural farmers.\n- Boundaries: image-based leaf classification only (no soil, climate, or pest analysis).\n- Platform: Android devices with TensorFlow Lite integration.\n- Offline functionality for areas with poor connectivity.\n\nSlide 8 û Expected Outcome\n- High-accuracy CNN models optimized for mobile.\n- Real-time disease detection and advisory recommendations.\n- Offline functionality for rural areas.\n- Improved farmer decision-making ? reduced crop loss.\n- Contribution to agricultural digitization in Ghana.\n\nSlide 9 û Timeline\n|  |  |  | \n|  |  |  | \n|  |  |  | \n|  |  |  | \n|  |  |  | \n|  |  |  | \n\n\n\nSlide 10 û References\n- Saleem, Potgieter, & Arif (2020). CNNs for plant disease classification.\n- Mariam Reda (2022). MobileNet/EfficientNet for mobile deployment.\n- Pineda Medina et al. (2024). MobileNetV2 potato disease detection.\n- ISS Africa (2025). Crop loss statistics in Ghana.\n- Siddiqua et al. (2022). Limitations of mobile plant disease apps.\n- Khan et al. (2025). Challenges in automated plant disease detection.\n- AgroCentric (2025). Ghana AI-powered crop disease detection.\n- Devpost (2025). AI-IoT crop monitoring in Ghana.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n- Input: Leaf image (camera/gallery)\n- Preprocessing: Resize (224╫224), normalization\n- Feature Extraction: CNN layers (MobileNetV2/EfficientNet-B0)\n- Classification: Probability vector ? disease label\n- Output: Predicted disease + advisory recommendation\n- Design: Arrows connecting each stage, icons for camera, gears (processing), brain (CNN), and mobile phone (output).\n\n\n- Mobile-based CNN system for crop disease detection.\n- Focus on six major crops using PlantVillage dataset.\n- Lightweight models (MobileNetV2, EfficientNet-B0) optimized for Android.\n- Offline functionality ensures accessibility in rural Ghana.\n- Advisory recommendations empower farmers to reduce losses and improve sustainability.\n\n\n- AI-driven mobile solutions can revolutionize agriculture in Ghana.\n- The proposed system is Specific, Measurable, Achievable, Relevant, and Time-bound (SMART).\n- Expected to reduce crop losses (~19.3%) and strengthen food security.\n- Provides scalable, farmer-friendly technology for rural communities.\n- Future scope: expand dataset coverage, integrate severity analysis, and extend to more crops.\n\n\n\n\n?? SMART Framing\n- Specific: Six crops, CNN-based mobile app, offline advisory.\n- Measurable: Accuracy ? 90%, latency ? 1s per image, farmer adoption rate tracked.\n- Achievable: Lightweight models (MobileNetV2, EfficientNet-B0) proven feasible on Android.\n- Relevant: Addresses GhanaÆs 19.3% crop loss challenge.\n- Time-bound: 6-month phased timeline (dataset ? training ? app ? testing ? deployment).\n\n?? Prince, I can now design the actual slides with visuals (charts for dataset distribution, CNN workflow diagram, Ghana crop loss stats, and system architecture flow). Do you want me to prepare those diagrams and layouts so you can present directly?\n\nDataset Overview: Total Images: 87,867,Training Set: 70,295 images (80%),Validation Set: 17,572 images (20%)\n','','','','84f0aa0a426ae8874eb0f4e06f0048cd1897b0e0d7fa401160ce53e1606ee816','537896ffe1fab6fe2fea30711fdd2d7d1f85697cab8b535fc7e3578ba0121e69','723648b152fb63e5fe5818b95d4211284e95a86a72cad2d0a7260b809fab0281','Goal: Reduce crop losses, improve farmer decision-making, promote sustainable agriculture\n\n- AI and deep learning revolutionizing agriculture.\n- CNNs outperform traditional ML in disease classification.\n- Problem: Farmers struggle with disease identification ? yield loss, improper pesticide use.\n- Objective: Build a mobile CNN-based system for accurate disease detection and advisory.\n1\n\n\n- Traditional methods: SVM, KNN, image processing ? limited accuracy.\n- CNN breakthroughs: PlantVillage dataset, >99% accuracy under controlled conditions.\n- Transfer learning: ResNet, MobileNet, EfficientNet improve generalization.\n- MobileNetV2: lightweight, efficient, 98.7% accuracy for potato diseases (Pineda Medina et al., 2024).\n- Limitation: performance drops in real-world field images.\n\nSlide 4 û Methodology\n- Dataset: PlantVillage (2,500+ images, multiple crops).\n- Data split: 60:20:20 (train, validation, test).\n- Models: MobileNetV2 (89% accuracy), EfficientNet-B0 (91.2% accuracy).\n- Optimizers: SGD baseline, Adam for improved convergence.\n- Deployment: TensorFlow Lite for mobile inference.\n- Architecture: Image acquisition ? preprocessing ? CNN classification ? result visualization.\n\nSlide 5 û Significance of the Study\n- Agriculture = 32 billion cedis contribution to GhanaÆs GDP (2024).\n- Crop losses ~19.3% due to diseases/post-harvest issues.\n- System reduces losses, strengthens food security.\n- Empowers rural farmers